
Home Cybersecurity Lab Architecture

1. Project Overview

The Home Cybersecurity Lab is a virtualized cybersecurity training environment designed to provide practical experience in network security, vulnerability assessment, system hardening, and security monitoring.

The laboratory runs on a Windows host operating system using Oracle VirtualBox.

2. Host Environment

| Component | Configuration |
|---|---|
| Host Operating System | Windows |
| Virtualization Platform | Oracle VirtualBox |
| Security Workstation | Kali Linux |
| Server Environment | Ubuntu Server LTS |
| Network Configuration | Isolated Virtual Network (planned) |

3. Virtual Machines

Kali Linux
Purpose:
- Security assessment workstation.
- Network discovery within the authorized lab.
- Vulnerability assessment of designated lab systems.
- Security testing and documentation.

Status: Installed.

Ubuntu Server
Purpose:
- Host lab services and applications.
- Provide a defensive Linux environment.
- Generate system logs for monitoring.
- Support security hardening exercises.

Status: Planned.

Wazuh Monitoring Server
Purpose:
- Centralized log collection.
- Security event monitoring.
- Detection and investigation of suspicious activity.

Status: Planned.

4. Network Architecture

The virtual machines will communicate through an isolated VirtualBox network.

The network will be configured to prevent unintended access to external systems.

Network configuration will be documented during Phase 2.

5. Security Principles

- All security testing will take place on authorized laboratory systems.
- Vulnerable applications will remain isolated from public networks.
- Administrative access will be restricted.
- VM snapshots will be used before major configuration changes.
- Security findings and remediation activities will be documented.

6. Project Phases

1. Virtualization environment setup.
2. Network configuration.
3. Authorized security assessment.
4. Security monitoring and log analysis.
5. Documentation and final evaluation.

7. Current Status

Kali Linux and Ubuntu Server are installed in Oracle VirtualBox on a Windows host.

The isolated lab network are pending setup.
